# Modifications to ART (art_illumina) as shipped in
# artsrcmountrainier20160605linuxtgz.tgz, applied by the top-level Makefile
# right after the tarball is unpacked.
#
# Apply with:  patch -p1 -d art_src_MountRainier_Linux/ < patches/art_illumina_gargammel.patch
#
# What it changes, all of it confined to art_illumina:
#
#   * Reproducibility.  -rs/--rndSeed already existed, but it fed the C library
#     rand(), whose stream is libc-specific.  The generator is now built in
#     (art_illumina_src/artrand.h) and reproduces glibc's rand() bit for bit,
#     so a fixed seed gives the same reads on every platform and existing
#     results are unchanged.
#
#   * gzip.  Input FASTA is read through zlib, so plain and gzipped references
#     both work with no flag.  -gz/--gzip (and -gzl for the level) compresses
#     the FASTQ/ALN/SAM output directly, removing the need for a separate gzip
#     pass over the reads.
#
#   * Pipes.  -i and the new --fq1/--fq2/--aln1/--aln2/--samFile options accept
#     "-", "/dev/stdin", "/dev/stdout", "/dev/fd/N" and "fd:N".  When reads go
#     to stdout the run summary moves to stderr.
#
#   * Speed, roughly 4x on gargammel's workload, with byte-identical output:
#     - the per-base quality draw resolves through a bucket table instead of
#       walking a std::map;
#     - output is block-buffered rather than flushed once per line by endl;
#     - FASTA parsing works on a large buffer instead of istream::get()/peek();
#     - ini_set() uses byte tables in place of toupper() and a switch;
#     - N-masking uses a flag array instead of a std::set;
#     - the reference is no longer read a second time to build @SQ headers
#       unless an ALN or SAM file is actually being written;
#     - floor()/ceil() on non-negative values no longer call into libm.
#
#   * Indel bug fix (seqRead.h, set_rate).  The table that decides how many
#     insertions/deletions a read gets was built from P(X > i) starting at i=1,
#     so index i held P(X >= i+2) and placing a single indel was gated on the
#     probability of needing two.  The realized indel rate was therefore some
#     250x below the -ir/-dr given: at the defaults only 0.003% of 75bp reads
#     carried an indel, against the ~1.5% the parameters imply.  The table now
#     starts at i=0.  This is the one change here that alters the reads: output
#     is no longer byte-identical to stock ART unless -ir/-dr/-ir2/-dr2 are 0.
#
